// GENERATED by scripts/gen-docs.mjs from docs/API.md. Do not edit.
export const DOCS_HTML = "<h1 id=\"tocsin-api\">Tocsin API</h1>\n<p>Base URL: <code>https://tocsin.sh</code>. Every answer is JSON in UTF-8 unless this page says otherwise. Reads need no account and no key.</p>\n<h2 id=\"endpoints\">Endpoints</h2>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Method and path</th><th scope=\"col\">What it answers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>GET /v1/health</code></td><td><code>{ &quot;ok&quot;: true, &quot;version&quot;: &quot;&lt;x.y.z&gt;&quot; }</code> when the worker is up.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/events</code></td><td>One page of the feed: <code>{ &quot;events&quot;: [...], &quot;next_cursor&quot;: &lt;int&gt;, &quot;has_more&quot;: &lt;bool&gt; }</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/events/{id}</code></td><td>One advisory by its Tocsin id. 404 when it does not exist.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/events/cve/{cve}</code></td><td>The earliest advisory, by feed cursor, that lists the CVE id (<code>CVE-YYYY-NNNN</code>) in any of its <code>cve_ids</code>, not only the first one. <code>GET /cve/{cve}</code> with <code>Accept: application/json</code> lists every such advisory. 400 for a malformed id, 404 when none.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /advisories/{id}</code></td><td>One advisory as an HTML page. HTML is the default: no <code>Accept</code> header, <code>*/*</code> and any <code>Accept</code> that names <code>text/html</code> get HTML. An <code>Accept</code> that names <code>application/json</code> (any q-value) and not <code>text/html</code> gets the advisory JSON. ETag with 304, <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=300</code>. 404 when it does not exist.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /cve/{cve}</code></td><td>Every advisory that carries a CVE id (any of its <code>cve_ids</code>), as one HTML page. <code>Accept: application/json</code> returns <code>{ &quot;cve&quot;, &quot;advisories&quot;: [...] }</code>. 404 when none.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /sitemap.xml</code></td><td>Every advisory page and every CVE page, with no <code>lastmod</code>. Past one file (50,000 URLs at most) it is an index of <code>/sitemap-{n}.xml</code> files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/check</code></td><td>Which runtimes are affected, from query parameters such as <code>?node=24.22.0&amp;php=8.4.26</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /v1/check</code></td><td>Which dependencies are affected, from lockfiles (multipart) or JSON.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /v1/status</code></td><td>Each enabled source with <code>last_run_at</code>, <code>last_ok_at</code> and <code>last_error</code>, plus the newest feed <code>cursor</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /.well-known/tocsin.json</code></td><td>The discovery document: every endpoint URL and the MCP URL.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /llms.txt</code></td><td>A plain-text guide for agents.</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /schema/advisory.v1.json</code></td><td>The JSON Schema of one advisory.</td></tr><tr><td>MCP <code>https://mcp.tocsin.sh/mcp</code></td><td>The remote MCP server (streamable HTTP).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"feed-filters\">Feed filters</h3>\n<p>All filters on <code>GET /v1/events</code> are optional.</p>\n<ul><li><code>since=&lt;cursor&gt;</code>: return events with a cursor above this value. Default 0.</li><li><code>ecosystem=&lt;csv&gt;</code>: OSV ecosystem or runtime name, for example <code>node,npm,PyPI</code>. At most 20 values.</li><li><code>component=&lt;csv&gt;</code>: package or runtime name. At most 20 values.</li><li><code>min_severity=critical|high|medium|low</code></li><li><code>exploited=true</code>: only advisories known to be exploited.</li><li><code>limit=1..100</code>: default 50.</li><li><code>order=asc|desc</code>: default <code>asc</code> (oldest first). With <code>desc</code>, <code>next_cursor</code> is the newest cursor on the page.</li></ul>\n<p>An invalid filter answers 400 with <code>{ &quot;error&quot;: &quot;&lt;reason&gt;&quot; }</code>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"check\">Check</h3>\n<p><code>GET /v1/check?node=24.22.0&amp;php=8.4.26</code> checks runtimes only. <code>POST /v1/check</code> takes one or more lockfiles as multipart fields, where the field name is the file name (<code>package-lock.json</code>, <code>npm-shrinkwrap.json</code>, <code>pnpm-lock.yaml</code>, <code>yarn.lock</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code>, <code>go.sum</code>, <code>composer.lock</code>, <code>Cargo.lock</code>, <code>Gemfile.lock</code>), or a JSON body:</p>\n<pre><code>curl -F &quot;package-lock.json=@package-lock.json&quot; https://tocsin.sh/v1/check\ncurl -H &quot;Content-Type: application/json&quot; -d &#39;{&quot;dependencies&quot;:[{&quot;ecosystem&quot;:&quot;npm&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;left-pad&quot;,&quot;version&quot;:&quot;1.3.0&quot;}],&quot;runtimes&quot;:{&quot;node&quot;:&quot;24.22.0&quot;}}&#39; https://tocsin.sh/v1/check</code></pre>\n<p>Runtime parameters are <code>node=</code>, <code>php=</code>, <code>python=</code>, <code>go=</code>, <code>deno=</code> and <code>bun=</code>. <code>go=</code> takes the Go toolchain version as <code>go version</code> prints it (<code>go=1.22.3</code> or <code>go=go1.22.3</code>). It matches the OSV <code>Go</code> advisories on the toolchain itself (package <code>stdlib</code>, <code>toolchain</code> or <code>cmd/&lt;tool&gt;</code>) by their OSV range events, and <code>fixed_in</code> is the lowest OSV <code>fixed</code> version above yours. Those advisories stay <code>Go</code> advisories for module matching; the runtime match does not add a second advisory. An affected item for <code>go=1.22.3</code> has <code>dependency</code> <code>{ &quot;ecosystem&quot;: &quot;go&quot;, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;go&quot;, &quot;version&quot;: &quot;1.22.3&quot; }</code>. The version is echoed as given: <code>go=go1.22.3</code> answers <code>&quot;version&quot;: &quot;go1.22.3&quot;</code>.</p>\n<p>The answer is <code>{ &quot;checked&quot;: &lt;int&gt;, &quot;affected&quot;: [...], &quot;skipped&quot;: [...], &quot;feed_cursor&quot;: &lt;int&gt; }</code>. Each affected item has <code>dependency</code>, <code>advisory_id</code>, <code>cve_ids</code>, <code>severity</code>, <code>exploited</code>, <code>fixed_in</code>, <code>action</code> and <code>url</code>, critical first, then exploited first. <code>skipped</code> lists what could not be checked; it is not a clean result. Send <code>feed_cursor</code> as <code>since=</code> to <code>/v1/events</code> to get every advisory published after the check.</p>\n<h3 id=\"status\">Status</h3>\n<p><code>GET /v1/status</code> answers:</p>\n<pre><code>{ &quot;sources&quot;: [{ &quot;id&quot;: &quot;osv&quot;, &quot;kind&quot;: &quot;osv&quot;, &quot;last_run_at&quot;: &quot;...&quot;, &quot;last_ok_at&quot;: &quot;...&quot;, &quot;last_error&quot;: null }], &quot;cursor&quot;: 1234 }</code></pre>\n<p><code>cursor</code> is the newest feed cursor, or 0 when the feed is empty. The same data is on the page <a href=\"/status\">/status</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"advisory-schema\">Advisory schema</h2>\n<p>Each event is one advisory. The schema is at <a href=\"/schema/advisory.v1.json\">/schema/advisory.v1.json</a>.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Field</th><th scope=\"col\">Type</th><th scope=\"col\">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>string</td><td>The Tocsin id.</td></tr><tr><td><code>cve_ids</code></td><td>string[]</td><td>CVE ids. Can be empty.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ghsa_id</code></td><td>string</td><td>GitHub advisory id, when there is one.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ecosystem</code></td><td>string</td><td>OSV ecosystem (<code>npm</code>, <code>PyPI</code>, <code>Go</code>, <code>Packagist</code>, <code>crates.io</code>) or runtime (<code>node</code>, <code>php</code>, <code>python</code>, <code>go</code>, <code>deno</code>, <code>bun</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>component</code></td><td>string</td><td>Package or runtime name.</td></tr><tr><td><code>affected</code></td><td>object[]</td><td>Version ranges: <code>introduced</code>, <code>fixed</code>, <code>last_affected</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>fixed_versions</code></td><td>string[]</td><td>Versions that fix it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>severity</code></td><td>object</td><td><code>label</code> (<code>critical</code>, <code>high</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>low</code>, <code>unknown</code>) and an optional <code>score</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>exploited</code></td><td>boolean</td><td>Known to be exploited.</td></tr><tr><td><code>epss</code></td><td>number</td><td>EPSS probability, when known.</td></tr><tr><td><code>published_at</code></td><td>string</td><td>ISO 8601 time.</td></tr><tr><td><code>modified_at</code></td><td>string</td><td>ISO 8601 time.</td></tr><tr><td><code>summary</code></td><td>string</td><td>One line from the source.</td></tr><tr><td><code>action</code></td><td>string</td><td>What to do, computed from the data (for example the fixed version).</td></tr><tr><td><code>references</code></td><td>string[]</td><td>Links.</td></tr><tr><td><code>sources</code></td><td>object[]</td><td>Each source record: <code>source</code>, <code>source_id</code>, <code>url</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"cursor-rule\">Cursor rule</h2>\n<ol><li>Store <code>next_cursor</code>.</li><li>Send it back as <code>since=&lt;next_cursor&gt;</code> on the next call.</li><li>Repeat while <code>has_more</code> is true. When <code>has_more</code> is false, you are up to date.</li></ol>\n<p>An empty page returns your own <code>since</code> as <code>next_cursor</code>, so you never lose your place. Each page has a strong <code>ETag</code>. Send it back in <code>If-None-Match</code>; an unchanged page answers 304.</p>\n<h2 id=\"rate-limits\">Rate limits</h2>\n<p>Anonymous calls are limited per IP per minute. The limits are settings rows, so they can change without a deploy. The defaults:</p>\n<ul><li><code>GET /v1/events</code>: 60 per minute (<code>feed.anon_rate_per_minute</code>).</li><li><code>/v1/check</code>: 20 per minute (<code>check.anon_rate_per_minute</code>).</li><li><code>POST /v1/check</code> body: 2 MB (<code>check.max_body_bytes</code>). Over the cap the answer is 413.</li></ul>\n<p>Over a limit the answer is 429 with <code>Retry-After</code> in seconds.</p>\n<h2 id=\"webhook-signature\">Webhook signature</h2>\n<p>Not live yet. Watch lists, API keys and webhook delivery are planned and not in the API today. The planned format: each delivery is a POST of the advisory JSON with these headers:</p>\n<ul><li><code>Tocsin-Event-Id</code>: the event id.</li><li><code>Tocsin-Timestamp</code>: the send time.</li><li><code>Tocsin-Signature: sha256=&lt;hex HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body, keyed with your webhook secret&gt;</code></li></ul>\n<p>Compute the HMAC over the raw body bytes and compare it with the header in constant time.</p>\n<h2 id=\"connect-command\">Connect command</h2>\n<pre><code>npx tocsin connect</code></pre>\n<p>The <code>tocsin</code> CLI (Node 20 or later) finds the agent tools on this machine and adds the <code>tocsin</code> MCP server (<code>https://mcp.tocsin.sh/mcp</code>) to each one: Claude Code (<code>~/.claude.json</code>, plus the Tocsin skill), Cursor (<code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code>), Claude Desktop (<code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>, through <code>npx -y mcp-remote</code>) and Codex (<code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>).</p>\n<p>Connect also installs the Tocsin skill for Codex (<code>~/.codex/skills/tocsin/SKILL.md</code>) and as a Cursor rule (<code>~/.cursor/rules/tocsin.mdc</code>).</p>\n<ul><li><code>--claude-code</code>, <code>--cursor</code>, <code>--claude-desktop</code>, <code>--codex</code>: wire only these tools.</li><li><code>--dry-run</code>: print the edits and write nothing.</li><li><code>--print</code>: print the MCP JSON block only.</li><li><code>--hook</code>: with Claude Code, also add a <code>SessionStart</code> hook to <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code>. The hook runs <code>npx -y tocsin check --summary</code>, which prints one line and never blocks the session.</li><li><code>--print-agents-md</code>: print a block for a repo&#39;s <code>AGENTS.md</code> and write nothing.</li></ul>\n<p>A second run changes nothing. Connect never writes a file it cannot parse, never replaces a <code>tocsin</code> entry that is already there and never replaces a skill copy that you edited. The same CLI has <code>npx tocsin check</code>, <code>npx tocsin latest</code> and <code>npx tocsin watch</code>.</p>\n<p>To add the server by hand in Claude Code:</p>\n<pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http tocsin https://mcp.tocsin.sh/mcp</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"codex\">Codex</h3>\n<pre><code>npx tocsin connect --codex</code></pre>\n<p>This adds the MCP server to <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> and the skill to <code>~/.codex/skills/tocsin/SKILL.md</code>. Codex also reads <code>AGENTS.md</code> in a repo. <code>npx tocsin connect --print-agents-md</code> prints this block for it:</p>\n<pre><code>## Security advisories (Tocsin)\n\nAt session start and before a deploy, run `npx tocsin check --json`.\nExit 1: a dependency has an advisory. Read `affected[]` and upgrade to `fixed_in`.\nExit 3: the check failed. Do not report the project as safe.\nDocs: https://tocsin.sh/docs</code></pre>";
